---
import InfoPageLayout from '../layouts/InfoPageLayout.astro';

const title = 'Characters & Story | Mystery Emblem, a Pokemon Fire Emblem Fan Game';
const description =
  'Meet the cast of Mystery Emblem: your Dragon hero, Quaxly, Flabebe, Quaquaval, Florges, King Serperior, and the allies joining your expedition.';
---

<InfoPageLayout title={title} description={description} heading="Characters & Story">
  <p>
    Ages ago, the Dragon Kingdom kept the world at peace until Hoopa tore open a Space-Time Rift and
    summoned ferocious Paradox Pokemon. Haxorus, Dragonite, and Goodra gave their last energy to seal
    the Rift, unaware Hoopa escaped through a closing portal, and hid away three Dragon Eggs: Dreepy,
    Deino, and yours.
  </p>

  <h2>Your hometown family</h2>

  <h3>You: the Dragon hero</h3>
  <p>
    A personality quiz decides which Dragon-type Pokemon hatches from your ancient egg:
    <strong>Axew</strong>, <strong>Bagon</strong>, <strong>Gible</strong>, <strong>Dratini</strong>,
    or <strong>Goomy</strong>. Raised in a peaceful Verdant Kingdom village by Quaquaval alongside
    Quaxly and Flabebe, you embark on a perilous journey when King Serperior sends an urgent summons.
  </p>

  <h3>Quaxly</h3>
  <p>
    Quaquaval's biological son and your upbeat, proud foster brother. Energetic, loyal, and always
    eager to prove his footwork in front of his dad.
  </p>

  <h3>Flabebe</h3>
  <p>
    Florges's daughter, your perceptive childhood friend, and the squad's dedicated healer. Both her
    blossom and her mother's match the aura color of whichever Dragon hero you become.
  </p>

  <h3>Quaquaval</h3>
  <p>
    Father to Quaxly, foster father to you, and secretly a former member of King Serperior's Royal
    Guard who laid down his cloak after his wife's fatal accident. He coaches your squad through
    <em>Quaquaval's Field Notes</em> and joins your playable roster as an experienced veteran.
  </p>

  <h3>Florges</h3>
  <p>
    Flabebe's warmhearted mother who tends the village homestead and sends her healing salves with
    your party when the royal summons arrives.
  </p>

  <h2>Act 1 expedition recruits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Smoliv:</strong> a timid traveler rescued from mountain foothills raiders who feels safest marching beside you.</li>
    <li><strong>Machop:</strong> an eager mountain guide filling in for a busy Machamp to lead you through a shortcut cavern.</li>
    <li><strong>Slakoth:</strong> a sleepy meadow dweller with Hidden Potential (+20% to all stat growths) in Paralogue 1.</li>
    <li><strong>Starly, Caterpie, and Pawmi:</strong> your three hometown sparring rivals who secretly follow you all the way to the capital gates to join the fight.</li>
    <li><strong>Honedge and Sandile:</strong> valiant warriors from the Steel Kingdom and Sand Kingdom assigned by King Serperior to guard your northern march.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Rulers, legends, and rivals across the 5 Acts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>King Serperior</strong> rules the Verdant Kingdom and coordinates with the Sand and Steel Kingdoms to uncover the truth behind the Rift.</li>
    <li><strong>Baxcalibur</strong> slumbers deep within the Ice Kingdom, holding ancient memories of the Dragon Kingdom's fall.</li>
    <li><strong>Drakloak / Dragapult</strong> and <strong>Hydreigon</strong> carry the legacies of the other two surviving Dragon Eggs.</li>
    <li><strong>Emperor Kingambit</strong> commands the Steel Kingdom's legions, while <strong>Hoopa</strong> plots from beyond the Space-Time Rift.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The six realms</h2>
  <p>
    Act 1 unfolds across the <strong>Verdant Kingdom</strong>, from your village training pitch and
    mountain caves to the Emerald Capital. Beyond lie the <strong>Sand Kingdom</strong>,
    <strong>Steel Kingdom</strong>, <strong>Ice Kingdom</strong>, <strong>Fire Kingdom</strong>, and
    <strong>Forest Tribe</strong>. Read more <a href="/about/">about the game</a>, or learn
    <a href="/how-to-play/">how to play</a>.
  </p>
</InfoPageLayout>
